{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-4-8","id":"msg_01WJLQu29BzXBRJon2FAUs21","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Anchor is a single-user personal productivity system that has grown a substantial R&D \"cockpit\" layer on top. Grounded in the project docs:\n\n**What it is**\n- A **personal productivity / GTD system for J.C. Liechty**, living entirely in one folder (`C:\\dev\\Anchor`) with **plain-markdown files as the source of truth** (DASHBOARD.md, PROJECTS.md, INBOX.md, domain files, etc.) â€” no database, no syncing.\n- Built as a **self-contained Python stdlib app** (`anchor_gui.py`) â€” a local web server on `http://localhost:8777` that renders an interactive dashboard and writes changes straight back to the markdown. It runs persistently as the Windows NSSM service `anchor`.\n\n**What it does**\n- **Task lifecycle management**: capture, add, edit, complete, cancel, save-for-later, restore â€” across domains (academic, commercial, family, writing). A mirror CLI (`anchor.py`) does the same and generates a static `dashboard.html`.\n- A daily **self-test** (`anchor_healthcheck.py`, 5 AM scheduled task) parses every file, exercises every endpoint, and walks the v2/v3/v4 R&D surfaces fully stubbed, writing a dated health report.\n- A **trio-driven R&D control surface** â€” the bulk of recent work. Each project gets a per-project \"cockpit\" window where the research â†’ planning â†’ build trio (researchPrime â†’ Crucible â†’ Foreman) runs as **persistent, isolated, server-side terminal sessions** (real ConPTY via the one allowed native dep `pywinpty`, per-session git-worktree isolation, xterm.js front-end), with cached/validated session+project summaries, cost/token/time rollups, and deliverable launch-by-type.\n\n**What it ships**\n- The declared deliverable is **`anchor_gui.py`** itself â€” the running dashboard server.\n- Latest milestone: **R&D Surface v4 \"Project Cockpit\"** (9 waves GREEN, built by Foreman, merged to master 2026-06-13; revision v4.1 rebuilt the project-window render to the locked Paradigm-2 design: lane tiles with status lights â†’ inline expanding panels with a split summary over a resizable terminal).\n\n**One caveat on grounding:** these claims are drawn from CLAUDE.md and the memory index, not re-verified against the current source this turn. If you want, I can confirm specific claims (e.g., that v4 is actually merged, or which deliverables are pinned) against the live files."}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":4410,"cache_read_input_tokens":45851,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":4410,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"output_tokens":2,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"54dcebfb-b361-4ed5-8d9f-a396204a583d","uuid":"b2caf2bd-9d4e-44e0-a9cb-cbd3e4f20d02","request_id":"req_011Cc2LPuQDiwobX7kDifx6h"}
